KPL/MYB

Diurnal and semidiurnal variations of the Earth orientation parameters that the daily IERS
series (EOP 20 C04, Bulletin A) do not contain: the effect of the ocean tides on polar motion
and UT1 and the libration (lunisolar torques on the triaxial Earth) in polar motion and UT1.
They are added to the interpolated daily values. Read by myb_eop_set_tides (myb/frames.h)
with the prefix 'IERS10_EOPT', in the series form of data/frames/iau2006-cip.tk.

Sources (IERS Conventions 2010, IERS Technical Note 36):
  ocean tides, Tables 8.2a, 8.2b (polar motion) and 8.3a, 8.3b (UT1), 71 terms: the table of
    subroutine PMUT1_OCEANS of the IERS program interp.f (Ch. Bizouard, after R. Eanes'
    ortho_eop.f), https://hpiers.obspm.fr/iers/models/interp.f,
    SHA-256 9ff5f893ac06c8d4123ec45cecde4df99f18cb2f3b19518bcd7494b6aa35b4e6;
  libration in polar motion, Table 5.1a, 10 diurnal terms: rows 16 .. 25 of PMSDNUT2.F,
    https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/content/chapter5/software/PMSDNUT2.F,
    SHA-256 0818b58bc2a420e1eb3f951d8a74646e5fe7b5371c9beb5e89fa37c12dd0d965;
  libration in UT1, Table 5.1b, 11 terms: UTLIBR.F (Brzezinski & Capitaine 2003),
    https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/content/chapter5/software/UTLIBR.F,
    SHA-256 f523335d552ac14b661121a081ad799382312d819853c674bc0102484b5e2406.
  Downloaded on 2026-11-09; coefficients copied without change (polar motion in
  microarcseconds, UT1 in microseconds). The LOD variations follow as -86400 dUT1/dt.

Arguments: chi = GMST + pi and the Delaunay arguments l, l', F, D, Omega, in arcseconds,
with t = (MJD - 51544.5) / 36525 from the UTC MJD of the EOP tables, as in the IERS
routines: GMST = 67310.54841 s + (8640184.812866 s + 3155760000 s) t + 0.093104 s t^2
- 6.2e-6 s t^3 (times 15 for arcseconds, plus 648000 for pi); the Delaunay arguments are
those of IERS Conventions 2010 eq. 5.43 (subroutine FUNDARG).

\begindata

